 was true he really is a hunter but he  hunts demons not animals he also really  did want to save innocent people but in  his mind the only way to save them is to  exterminate all demons so ardberg really  was sincere the whole time just not in  the way that anne had anticipated this  kind of shows the limitations of anne's  lie detecting powers in a very  interesting way ardberg explains to our  heroes that they are just too young to  understand the truth about the demons  they don't know what happened during the  holy war and how many innocent people  were mercilessly slaughtered by the  demon clan entire families were wiped  out parents lost their own innocent  children because of demons and so the  only way to protect humanity from  further suffering in the future is to  eliminate the entire demon clan percival  is still struggling with the beast  because he just can't cut through the  horns but sin has a suggestion he tells  percival to infuse his dragon handle  sword with his hope magic which ends up  increasing the power of his sword  exponentially with his newly boosted  weapon percival is able to cut off the  horns with ease after being nearly eaten  at one point percival manages to defeat  the beast with an assist from nazians  our heroes then prepare to take on  ardberg himself but when they turn  around they realize that he's already  running away at full speed he tries to  play it cool and call it a strategic  retreat which reminds me of my boy  joseph joestar so i have to give artberg  respect for that now technically the  gang could just leave artberg and  continue their journey to leonis but  purse will insist that they must rescue  his demon friends from ardberg's crystal  seal the fact that percival wants to  rescue the villagers even after learning  that they are actually demons surprises  the elder but percival insists that the  fact that some demons did bad things in  the past doesn't mean that all of them  are bad just like the fact that his  father killed his grandfather doesn't  mean that all humans are bad if you're a  good guy it doesn't matter whether  you're a human or a demon this seems to  really warm the elder's heart and he  decides to place his faith in percival  and the others the gang follows artberg  to a cavernous crystal grotto that turns  out to be a giant maze and of course it  is also a trap artberg's magic is not  good for direct battles so he is not a  fighter but if he can trap his opponents  in a specific way he can use his magic  to defeat them his magic is the ability  to revert all living things within a  50-yard radius into their infant forms  and that is exactly what happens to  percival naciennes ann and donny they  are turned into adorable little toddlers  who can barely walk on their own  needless to say they are now in no  condition to fight they're just babies  after all and that means that aardberg  has won well percival is still  freakishly strong even as a baby so he  turns out to be a bit bothersome but at  the end of the day he has still mentally  reverted to a baby so he isn't really  hard to beat however things change when  anne begins to cry she weeps and begs  artberg not to hurt her friends in this  moment little crying anne reminds  artberg of his own young daughter his  daughter who it turns out was brutally  murdered by demons during the holy war  that is why artberg is so committed to  destroying the demon clan they killed  his innocent young daughter for no  reason and so he concluded that all  demons must be evil monsters he decided  to avenge his daughter while also making  sure that no other humans suffer his  tragic fate in the future so he  dedicated his life to exterminating all  demons and that is about the time that  the elder suddenly appears inside the  grotto he tells artberg that he now  understands why the holy knight is doing  what he's doing the elder also knows  that artberg desperately longs to meet  his daughter again artberg denies this  at first but then the elder offers him a  deal if artberg reverses the spell that  he placed on percival and the others and  if he gives back the crystal with the  demons the elder will let him meet his  daughter again artberg doesn't believe  that this is even possible at first but  he can tell that something is off with  the elder he was not sealed away in the  crystal so he is not a demon but the  baby spell also doesn't work on him for  some reason so he's probably not human  either the elder says that according to  the rules of artberg's magic it takes  one minute for someone to get younger by  one year so for percival and the others  it only took 16 minutes to turn them  into babies but the elder explains that  due to the fact that he is over three  thousand years old it would take three  whole days for ardberg's spell to work  on him the elder then strikes a  flamboyant pose that reveals his true  identity that's right the elder is not a  demon or a human he is none other than  the goat sin of lust gother now it makes  sense why the elder made that connection  between sin the fox and the fox's sin of  greed although the part about gother  putting sin to sleep doesn't make much  sense and neither does gother's choice  of wardrobe but moving on goether  introduces himself as one of the seven  deadly sins the so-called sworn enemies  of king arthur what a freaking twist  even though i suspected that something  was off about the elder i definitely did  not expect him to turn out to be one of  the original seven deadly sins and yes  it's our boy gother i guess gother  became the elder because he decided to  help those peace-loving demons who are  essentially refugees from the demon  realm but who are also feared and hated  by everyone in the human realm artberg  knows that he doesn't stand a chance of  defeating one of the seven deadly sins  so he decides to just run for it he  still believes that killing percival is  the right thing to do because if one of  the four knights of the apocalypse is  allowed to live he will eventually  destroy the world once gother catches up  to artberg the holy knight orders him to  stay away or he will throw baby percival  and baby anne into a canyon and kill  them but then golther shows artberg that  he is holding ardberg's own daughter an  adorable little baby girl and he then  asks artberg if he would really kill  percival and anne in front of his own  daughter now the little girl is just a  vision that gotha created from artberg's  memories and artberg knows that it's  just a mirage but it is so realistic  that he can't help but cry tears of joy  he agrees to lift the spell on percival  and the others and he recalls what  happened after he lost his daughter all  those years ago his powers only awoke  after he lost his daughter they seemed  to have been triggered by the tragic  event and after that king arthur came to  him and asked him whether he wants to  see his daughter again alive and well if  so then he must join arthur and lend him  his powers even though artberg thought  this was a ridiculous proposition the  look in arthur's eyes convinced him that  the king was serious so wait does this  mean that arthur knows of a real way to  revive the dead if so then this is a  massive reveal that is going to be  extremely important later on so artberg  agreed to serve king arthur and he  embraced arthur's mission to banish all  the demons and make the world safe for  humanity hardbrook says that he sees the  light now no one can really bring back  the dead and his daughter is gone but he  appreciates go through allowing him to  see his daughter one last time just the  way he had remembered her then out of  nowhere gother senses that two spears  infused with magic are flying right at  them and they seem to be targeting  percival golther is able to save  percival using an epic acrobatic  maneuver but after golther takes  percival out of harm's way the second  spear is heading straight for baby anne  artberg tells his daughter or the vision  of his daughter to hold on a sec because  daddy will be coming to see her soon he  then rescues anne by lifting her over  his shoulders and out of harm's way but  at the cost of the spear piercing right  through his own torso artberg sacrifices  his life to save anne and his last words  to her are to grow up and be a great  woman wow the twists in this arc are  just insane the villagers are demons the  honest and sincere hunter guy is a  holding out of camelot who wants to kill  percival the village elder is actually  gother and then in the end artberg  sacrifices his life to save anne in what  ends up being a wholesome and  heartbreaking moment i have to say that  i was really impressed by this arc and  there is a lot of depth here in the  early stages of the original seven  deadly sin story our impressions of the  demons and especially those low level  demons is almost exclusively negative  and yet in life things are never so  simple and there are indeed good and bad  demons just like there are good and bad  humans i'm so glad that the sequel story  decided to explore this topic and  artberg ended up being such a freaking  interesting character on the one hand  his decision to target all demons and  even percival just because of his  preconceived assumptions is clearly bad  and yet you can see where he's coming  from after you learn his tragic  backstory after all some demons really  are monsters just like some humans are  monsters as well and artberg had the bad  luck to meet some of those evil demons  first hand those evil demons then  informed his opinion of all demons and  yet now we meet demons who literally  risked their lives to avoid killing  humans they had to flee the demon realm  because refusing to fight in the holy  war was the same as treason from the  perspective of the demon clan and on top  of all of that we have gother just  hanging out with the demons and  protecting them this makes sense since  golthar's creator the original golter  was also a demon who wanted peace and  opposed the holy war so by protecting  these demons gother is honoring the  memory of his creator but that epic  reveal aside what will gother do now  will he continue just chilling in the  demon village or will he now join our  heroes on their journey also did gother  figure out sin's true identity and is  sin actually bond if so will we see  bonds human form soon oh and who was  that bride from sin's strange vision is  she related to the fact that arthur is  currently looking for a bride finally  who sent those magic spears after  percival man so many interesting  questions this was easily the best arc  of the sequel manga so far and how funny  would it be if it turned out that sin  really was bon all along i know a lot of  fans were complaining that nakaba should  have featured the original sins more  prominently in the sequel manga so how  hilarious would it be if bon was  actually there the whole time definitely  let me know what you guys think about  the return of golfer this current arc of  the manga and sins true identity down in  the comments below i always love hearing  from you if you guys enjoyed this video  and you want to see more seven deadly  sins and four nights of the apocalypse  content here on the channel just leave a  quick like and comment it only takes a  second but it really helps with the  youtube algorithm and if you're new to  the channel or you watch our videos but  you just haven't taken the time to  subscribe yet do me a quick favor and  make this the video that you subscribe  hit the bell and then select the option  that says all if you don't do that  you're going to miss a ton of our videos  in the future it's just the way youtube  works you can also hit me up on twitter  and instagram at animeopror a big thank  you to all of our anime uproar patrons  who make videos like this one possible  special thank you to alpha sigma this  man is an absolute mad lad and 